<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel live: Eisenkot party submits bill to new parliament to investigate October 7 failures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f31aa1728da7c5d539c05f8ad9867cddd033810b8294f9bbf6cb49d7b5c858</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:40:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-live-new-israeli-parliament-sworn-in-eisenkot-aims-to-form-government-netanyahu-knesset" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament was sworn in Tuesday with opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot aiming to build a coalition after receiving a mandate to form a government. Eisenkot's party moved to immediately set up a commission to investigate failures that allowed Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, a move long resisted by caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Follow our live coverage for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>New Israel parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot works to form new govt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b56fda5b90f8e197979adad0dab832743f39d102f3e1fd44c3e4a849465b50dc</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt--82de353b7556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament will be sworn on Tuesday, November 10, with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu set to lose his majority as rival Gadi Eisenkot works to form a new government. The opposition hopes to use its newfound legislative power to move quickly on key priorities, including a commission to investigate security failures under Netanyahu that allowed the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's new parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot prepares government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecd10d3a3f9028f2718907f6b6114bf8fc88ea9d98db6963def2158c30b4e19c</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T09:17:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-israel-s-new-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-forms-government--637eebbf9862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-israel-s-new-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-forms-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament is set to be sworn in Tuesday with neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc nor opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot's camp holding a majority. Eisenkot seeks to build a coalition after receiving a mandate to form a government.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Will Eisenkot succeed in 'minefield of Israeli politics' where 'so many other generals' have failed?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a66a82898c17b7e17990ce353dbfb6585f713ef77bb0155b3378effb9307f176</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-fa--ea02cbc16553.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-failed" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Dahlia Scheindlin, Israeli political analyst, strategic consultant and pollster, to examine a question that reaches far beyond the immediate struggle for power: Can Israel move beyond PM Benjamin Netanyahu amid coalition deadlock, growing disillusionment in Washington and the persistent limits of political inclusion?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'We think' the Iranians and Americans want to negotiate, Egyptian FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f91abdd832e274910d2de88e5f19a1fededc460ba19d3c0f8c87fcb0645bf3b0</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:31:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says--3e2f1e24b9a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian Foreign Minister Badr Abdelatty said he believed Iran and the United States wanted to negotiate, but called for a "concrete deal" to prevent another escalation. He also said Cairo was still "counting" on US President Donald Trump to "move forward" with the stalled Gaza peace plan and was "confident" US military aid to Egypt would continue.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf25fac92721a28ed87c0918d624ee3a733f2aefe3f27a31a6fb81a8548013ad</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T17:26:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians--d44b8a8693f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran 'has mistaken perception' of US midterm result, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1eb7fa9cfe5cccc58f8966ead944a8556916ecc5bb879f929ea639837dd96a</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:49:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says--83d8e60dc207.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says" /><summary type="html">A leading commentator on Iran says the country sees the results of the US midterm elections as giving them a golden opportunity for a sweet deal. Paymon Azmoudeh from Forward Global was speaking amid conflicting statements from the key players about whether there will be further US military action in Iran. President Donald Trump says that renewed strikes on Iran are "highly unlikely" if talks progress. However, Iran's foreign minister says the midterms have brought a ⁠pause to mediators' work.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia intercepts Houthi missiles as Riyadh's Aramco building damaged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f75f4f65c8ec849a4d831b60839a3b5e55bc6ec27fe298c4ae5af2c2e4cfafc3</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:41:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged--908b03ae8d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia intercepted incoming missiles from Yemen's Houthi rebels targeting the kingdom's capital and other regions on Sunday, November 8, with falling debris damaging a building belonging to the state-owned oil giant Aramco in Riyadh’s financial district.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has six weeks to form a government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a386bc55d73c1038131281abe5307a69e7fc0a82bfc6bccf630c065c764ff695</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:36:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government--4fa49cb09b7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog formally gave opposition politician Gadi Eisenkot the first chance to form the next government Sunday evening, leaving Eisenkot six weeks to try to put together a coalition to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc4974c0e9182bb11a4ea0c8bf24f30b84bf344730dc5b4e46ef28677e49f66e</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T21:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government--f27d5923499e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e835fd7a2b70191bdcbca0d962044390f2e6a01799b7b8bfa67440ba5b5164d8</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:58:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government--3797dae49af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1f0433e92837a19a42945ceb4edc0e386b19b35a4d346bc75811d54bde945b2</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:22:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens--95e6e91a4caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens" /><summary type="html">One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6788f24e1785dca40e7e688cdf0d8b9509086950cbbcdb7e01f4a0816111d6c</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:47:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-ne--c83bf488fa4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 27 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8918e7ff6ad182ccd2f69ed346640ffd77e52f169a81f8a7e3f55a57117256ad</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:43:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence--0c9b38b79b08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence" /><summary type="html">Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2238a31ab76de30907ba6c4eaf48ce13ddfd83676415c5de639d3b685dcf621e</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:42:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents--9e19bbe6af60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents" /><summary type="html">Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim attack on Aramco skyscraper in Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:040fe2268f7a1eb13ea8421038c1dc3ca34840a7d66f54120643e70c6eb81244</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T08:11:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-yemen-s-houthis-claim-attack-on-aramco-building-in-riyadh-s-financial-district--fcf5a21a0bd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-yemen-s-houthis-claim-attack-on-aramco-building-in-riyadh-s-financial-district" /><summary type="html">A skyscraper belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco was hit by a Houthi-claimed attack on Sunday, blowing out windows across several floors but causing no casualties. The Iran-aligned group has repeatedly targeted Aramco facilities and infrastructure.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b26fd3390e48f159d3ce53780ce99a6c7ae1687b02aa5bc7d6847c8ba92dcf96</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog picked former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to try to form a government, he said in a statement Saturday. Last month's parliamentary elections left neither Eisenkot nor Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu with a clear path to building a majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel coalition talks gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e247ba34f55cadb6989a4a33460c004d84f503718428465fa38e3adcbab9a91</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum--e112145ab913.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Following inconclusive elections in Israel, opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot says he is confident of securing the mandate to form a government, as President Isaac Herzog prepares to nominate the first candidate. Eisenkot claims he is making progress in efforts to oust long-serving Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 30 dead in strikes on Taiz market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:081033a2e3721af850ba7d30f08afc7d4e5312a4f2d86b841dab49d63d833bbb</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:37:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market--556471887193.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market" /><summary type="html">At least 30 people have reportedly been killed in an attack on a market in Yemen’s Taiz province, with Houthi rebels blaming Saudi airstrikes. Government forces and local authorities have disputed the claim, instead accusing the Houthis of indiscriminate fire. The province has witnessed intense clashes in recent weeks and is home to around half of the more than 300,000 people displaced by the latest fighting. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Is Israel opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot going to replace Benjamin Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23968e87f9b4da53d2efba870498f4ee1be56468af11c23381a455e555d41120</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:25:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu--06fb66f266f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">In Israel, Gadi Eisenkot emerged on Thursday, November 5, as the frontrunner to be tasked with forming a government. This comes after one of the two main parties representing ultra-Orthodox Jewish voters – a longtime ally of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition – declined to recommend any candidate for the task. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot claims 'progress' in coalition talks as opposition eases on ultra-Orthodox draft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8dc5f0ad07d5b6512a0087fed4a0d80ef04c84a5eeef0d092b62b19922e4277</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:43:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ult--688a89e5ca21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ultra-orthodox-draft" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot said on Friday he was making "significant progress" in forming a government to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu as one of his possible coalition partners walked back demands that ultra-Orthodox Jews complete military service and signalled a willingness to hold talks with the community.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel president to announce Sunday who will form new government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea76534cdedd841f05d5323db0f0429dcdca10a4cde3a45b443ed85c7d1692e6</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:39:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-israel-president-to-announce-sunday-who-will-form-new-government--374dc14e89f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-israel-president-to-announce-sunday-who-will-form-new-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he will announce on Sunday, November 8, whom he will task with trying to form a new government, following post-election talks with all party leaders. 46 parliament members recommended Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, while 67 backed his opponent Gadi Eisenkot. Seven lawmakers abstained.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu rival Eisenkot secures broad backing in bid to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d76895ea43ba1f3dc772ff13c76a0f29a23f79144b9f66be1cfcff101a4da02</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:02:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-netanyahu-rival-eisenkot-secures-broad-backing-in-bid-to-form-government--998e5f20ee41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-netanyahu-rival-eisenkot-secures-broad-backing-in-bid-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he will announce on Sunday, November 8, whom he will task with trying to form a new government, after the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot secured a commanding number of recommendations to replace Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Arab list backs Eisenkot as Netanyahu loses ultra-Orthodox support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc9d04fd949a6f844cd4becf5fa591627471cbf6f479f4657a0bd7af570d5cc7</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:43:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election--3aadbd4431d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-israel-main-arab-list-backs-eisenkot-to-form-government-after-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's largest Arab party grouping said Thursday it would recommend opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot to form the next government, potentially bolstering his bid after Arab-majority lists won a record 19 seats in last week's election and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lost the support of an allied religious party.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi missiles fired at Medina intercepted, Saudi coalition says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1f41139b704871b8d36365e3d0aae7c0a29a46af5df4bd977915b39ecea2ba2</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:07:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says--19ce0f207758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261105-houthi-missiles-fired-at-medina-intercepted-saudi-coalition-says" /><summary type="html">A ballistic missile fired at the Saudi city of Medina, one of Islam's holiest cities, was intercepted Thursday, a spokesman for the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthi rebels said. The announcement came shortly after the kingdom's civil defence agency warned of potential danger around the strategic port of Yanbu.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu claims 'serious concerns' of foreign spending to sway Israeli election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cd2309667ee18517ca7a67146c32e740ad5ed62e348a6d7e3978f293b45db95</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election--38bacb102ad6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-netanyahu-claims-serious-concerns-of-foreign-spending-to-sway-israeli-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Wednesday cited "serious suspicions" around foreign interference in Israel's recent parliamentary elections. He claims foreign countries spent large amounts of money to influence the results, while the largest Arab-Israeli bloc called such accusations "political persecution".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Iran's deputy parliament speaker reacts to Trump's elections setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a7aec2b60c9587f21615403a7bb9a3a549d1d9821bd89d659800d4b2c70d11d</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:50:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1--b3baa850b100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-iran-s-deputy-parliament-speaker-reacts-to-trump-s-elections-setback-1" /><summary type="html">First Deputy Speaker of the Parliament of Iran Ali Nikzad on Wednesday attributed Republican losses in the US midterm elections to Washington's war with Iran, telling lawmakers that American efforts to pressure Tehran had failed.  Democrats won control of both chambers of Congress in Tuesday's midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>What consequences for Israel as Democrats win the US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd8f8043732b30d7251a1fb5ee8704c8cef83635568a8851a9fdb11648a9a7e</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T11:32:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections--b88554bea6f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-what-consequences-for-israel-as-democrats-win-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Democrats seized control of the US Congress on Tuesday, capturing the Senate and House of Representatives in a stunning upset. What are the potential consequences for Israel and Benjamin Netanyahu, as Trump announced on Tuesday that the US will halt $3.8 billion in aid to the country? FRANCE 24's correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Four oil tankers destroyed in Hormuz after hitting mines, Tehran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40d7e3db4f9b487ecac6caddba5a2493e44447f24d79e268118d9642a305efc9</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T08:43:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-four-oil-tankers-destroyed-in-hormuz-after-hitting-mines-tehran-says--117c71d9585d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-four-oil-tankers-destroyed-in-hormuz-after-hitting-mines-tehran-says" /><summary type="html">Four oil tankers caught fire after hitting mines in the Strait of Hormuz, Tehran claimed Wednesday, a day after US President Donald Trump said the United States had launched strikes on Iran. Discussions to end the war between Washington and Tehran via mediators have continued with little sign of diplomatic breakthrough.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's President Herzog accepts certified election results, urges compromise to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:193db8dcd05088f4a076c1c87aab29587142261d21e21533e8cd2b437bff61e3</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T02:05:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-israel-s-herzog-urges-compromise-to-form-government-after-divisive-election--72801d1bfaac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261104-israel-s-herzog-urges-compromise-to-form-government-after-divisive-election" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Wednesday formally accepted the certified results from last week’s legislative elections which delivered no clear winner, and said he would begin consultations regarding the formation of a new government. Both Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his main challenger, former military chief Gadi Eisenkot, are negotiating to form a governing coalition.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
